From 15d2dee76354343c8ed8c92534f0eb5074c6a58e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 13:38:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tennis): UX fixes for MonoTennisLiveScore (#109)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add a serving indicator (●) derived purely from match state — flips per
  game and every 2 points in a tiebreak (deriveServer, cumulative parity).
- Render game/set milestone toasts via React state + an aria-live <output>
  so they are actually announced (was direct DOM injection, invisible to AT).
- Add a completed-set history strip, matching MonoSetsLiveScore.
- Standardize the aria-live region as a polite, atomic <output>; include
  serving + milestone context.
- Visually distinguish destructive Discard (mono-btn-danger) from Finish.
- Guard currentSetData (fallback to a blank set) so a completed/undone set
  no longer crashes the render.
- Mirror the derived server into the live-broadcast snapshot (servingTeam),
  same as the sibling sets scorer — no new mirrored action since serve is a
  pure function of the score.

Closes #109

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
